  "artifactWindow": "2026-09-02 two-stage within-family Orbium inverse, 2026-10-18 corrected-engine regeneration of the shape and movement analysis, 2026-10-19 corrected-engine damage assay and Orbium replay",
  "engine": "Corrected-engine entries ran on LeniaCLI build 060e90a71ec1, which contains the fixed Flow Lenia spatial-derivative stencil. The Orbium inverse uses additive Lenia, which has no derivative step; its replay on that build reproduced all 900 recorded frames byte for byte.",
  "correctionNote": "Version 3 of this report also reported a supplied-body maintenance search, intrinsic-dimension and local-sensitivity estimates of rule fibers, a conditional proposal model with refinement, a runtime cross-check, an endpoint landscape and canalization test, and a shape and movement result that was later reversed. They were computed with a Python port of Flow Lenia and with the main engine before its spatial-derivative stencil was fixed; both computed the gradient negated and with its axes swapped. Those results and their sources were removed.",
  "caseStudyNote": "The two-stage Orbium inverse was run on 2026-09-02 inside the qd24_additive_v1 family, with R, m, and s hidden from both search stages. The 2026-09-01 organic descriptor rerun and the warm-start archive map were withdrawn because the batched initializer grew each candidate from a different random starting field. The earlier cross-runtime Flow Lenia comparison was removed.",
